WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.802
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:05.972
-Speaking of the ocean...

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.674
[ Laughter ]

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:11.243
...two weeks ago,
we made a joke about peeing

00:00:11.243 --> 00:00:15.548
on a jellyfish sting
as a means of pain relief.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.551
We were told that is a myth.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.021
It won't actually provide
any pain relief

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:24.290
if you urinate
on a jellyfish sting.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:30.929
And this was actually the myth
was begun, was started...

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:34.600
By Jacques Cousteau...

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.570
on his short-lived...

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.673
1960s prank show "Jacque'd."

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:44.777
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:50.116
Uh, worth, uh, the wait.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.584
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.584 --> 00:00:55.455
We are off and running.
I made a joke in "A Closer Look"

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:58.258
that Henry Winkler
stole the Fonzie jacket,

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.360
and someone said
he couldn't have stolen

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.895
the black leather Fonzie jacket,

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.997
because he,
Henry Winkler himself,

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:08.201
brought that jacket
to the "Happy Days" set

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.303
from a previous film
he had done,

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.004
called "Lords of Flatbush."

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.407
He did this because he actually
thought the original jacket,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.841
which was sort
of a red windbreaker,

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:19.145
wasn't cool enough
to play Fonzie.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.014
So apologies to Henry Winkler.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:24.383
He did not steal the jacket
from the set of "Happy Days."

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.920
He stole it from the set
of "Lords of Flatbush."

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.521
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.521 --> 00:01:31.891
All jokes aside,
Henry, who we love

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.794
-- we love Henry --
he recently auctioned off

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.829
one of the original
Fonzie jackets

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.698
to raise money
for a great charity

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.766
called This Is About Humanity.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:42.669
Do check that charity out.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:45.004
Maybe make a donation.
It's a great cause.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:48.074
Henry is not just
one of our favorite guests,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.475
one of our favorite actors,

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:52.344
he is a wonderful human being

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:55.782
who will steal from sets.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.684
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:01.587
I guess I also incorrectly
called his character

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.590
"the Fonzie."

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.758
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.760
Um, it's either --

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.597
Obviously, it's either
"Fonzie" or "the Fonz."

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:16.936
It was, though -- It was --
It was -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.005
It was "the Fonzie"
on the Russian remake

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.307
of "Happy Days," called, um...

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:24.577
"This Days, While Not Happy,
Are Still Days."

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:28.347
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:33.419
Who can -- Who can forget
that iconic theme song?

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:34.820
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.255
[ Russian accent ] ♪ Monday,
Tuesday, these are days ♪

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:39.325
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.261
♪ Wednesday, Thursday,
also days ♪

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:45.131
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.699
[ Normal voice ] Hey, this is
a lovely gift someone sent me.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.834
Did you guys know, this whole
time we've been doing this,

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.637
there is a New Jersey Jackals,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:55.708
are an independent baseball team
that I think we're in Montclair

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:59.645
and now moving to Paterson,
New Jersey, next year.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:01.114
And I guess, because
they were moving,

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:04.417
there was sort of a fire sale
on Jackal merch.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:07.119
And so I,
I got this little fella here,

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:08.888
and I think he's just gonna be
a fun addition

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.389
to the whole
"Corrections" family.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:12.057
You know, I'll say things like,

00:03:12.057 --> 00:03:14.527
"Are you enjoying
'Corrections?'"

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.895
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:18.998
And that's what we call
a special-effects budget.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.700
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.137
We mentioned a worm
in a bottle of tequila.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.805
We were told it would be mescal.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:29.008
While it's often misrepresented
as a worm,

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.244
it's a moth larvae.

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.712
But I will say, I've had
some mescal in my day.

00:03:33.712 --> 00:03:36.249
If you drink enough,
you can't taste the difference.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.017
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:42.855
We had a joke about
the life expectancies --

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:48.094
life expectancy --
of, um, men in America.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.562
And we said it's currently
76.1 years old.

00:03:50.562 --> 00:03:52.332
This was the graphic we showed.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:55.067
And somebody said, very fairly,
this is a terrible graphic

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.971
because if where the arrow
is now is at 76.1,

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.874
that means that
the original life expectancy

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:05.210
is, like, over
a thousand years old.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.645
So thank you for that heads-up.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:10.382
We do like to get
our graphics right.

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:14.587
Nobel laureate.
I pronounced it "laur-ee-ott."

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.223
That's a bummer to get wrong,
'cause it's a smart thing.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.991
And if you want to seem
like a smart person

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:21.660
and you call it
a Nobel "laur-ee-ott,"

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.095
kind of playing yourself.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.998
And I was making fun
of somebody else.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:29.468
It's a bad look.

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.671
It's like saying, "Check out
that rocket 'sky-en-tist.'"

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:34.373
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.675
Ooh.

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:38.611
We named some Minnesota towns.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:42.915
I said "Owa-toh-na."
It's "Owa-ton-na."

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.484
This was based on the fact
that Mike Lindell

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:48.787
got arrested
at a Hardee's in Mankato,

00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:51.591
and then we said
an Arby's in Owatonna.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.892
Got to get it right.
And then we said

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:56.695
a Jack in the Box in Oconomowoc.

00:04:56.695 --> 00:05:00.199
At the time,
we have a fantastic producer

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.934
at the show, named Emily,
and Emily said,

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.803
"Just FYI, there's not
a Jack in the Box in
Oconomowoc."

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:07.306
And we were all like,
"Nobody's gonna say anything."

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.141
Y'all did.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:11.911
Guess we've got a large amount
of viewers from Oconomowoc

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.712
who were very upset
about the fact that their town

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:14.914
doesn't have a Jack in the Box,

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.716
because a lot of you came out
and said that.

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:19.385
The problem is, "a
Jack in the Box in Oconomowoc"

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.153
is just too much fun to say.

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:23.656
And we weren't going to
let the facts

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:26.091
get in the way of our fiction.
We just liked it.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:28.394
It was also late-breaking,
I should say.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.929
It was a Fuddruckers
in Lake Minnetonka.

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:33.298
And then, about 5 minutes
before showtime,

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:36.836
Baze came up with "a
Jack in the Box in Oconomowoc,"

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.638
the same way Baze always does.

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:41.307
You think he's
asleep or dead, and...

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.743
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:46.445
...we're trying to come up --
and he just sort of rises up.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:49.649
"A Jack in the Box
in Oconomowoc."

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:53.386
And then, while we're laughing,
he just very slowly...

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:55.054
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.456
But I just wouldn't
be too picky,

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.624
because a lot of people say,
"Oh, 'Late Night'

00:05:58.624 --> 00:05:59.826
is so political these days.

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:02.328
Why can't you all be
more like Johnny Carson?"

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:05.264
A Jack in the Box in Oconomowoc
is the most Johnny Carson thing,

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:08.935
I feel like,
we said in a long time.

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:11.504
[ As Carson ] "A Jack in the Box
in Oconomowoc.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:15.041
Have you been to Oconomowoc?

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:19.878
Go to Oconomowoc,
walk walk off your economo.

00:06:19.878 --> 00:06:22.181
Do you get that?
Do you like that, Ed?"

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:24.016
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.751
[ Normal voice ] I think
you have to hold the base.

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.219
We're learning.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:28.720
Well, get a get
a close-up, Alex.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.289
Don't miss this gold.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:35.027
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:38.164
Alright. Alright.

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:43.502
Ooh. Talked about if you found
a survivor on<i> The Titanic.</i>

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:45.471
And I said,
"Wouldn't it be a fun --

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:48.241
A great screenplay would be
if there had been a survivor

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.142
who was 110 years old
and you went down

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:52.545
and you had to decide,
would you bring them up?"

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:55.047
A lot of people said, "Well,
it actually sank 110 years ago,

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.683
so a survivor would have to
at least be 111 years old."

00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:02.154
But other than that,
the screenplay is perfect.

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:04.557
You guys, it turns out
there was a movie --

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:09.828
a TV movie in 1981 --
with that basic plot,

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:11.096
called "Goliath Awaits."

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:12.531
Did you ever see
"Goliath Awaits," Shoemaker?

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:14.433
Does that ring any bells?

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:17.636
It would have been the kind
of movie you'd watch,

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:19.605
because it wasn't on cable.
Um...

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:22.174
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:26.178
Mark Harmon.
Eddie Albert, Christopher Lee,

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:29.414
and it was basically
some oceanographers.

00:07:29.414 --> 00:07:30.950
They find a shipwreck.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.118
And our friend --
good old friend, Mark Harmon,

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:34.854
goes down and, I guess,
through a porthole,

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:37.523
sees a beautiful woman
and goes back

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.525
and he says, "There must be
an air bubble or something,

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.193
because there are some survivors
on<i> The Goliath.'"</i>

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:42.628
That was the name
of the ship.

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:43.996
And, well, I don't
have to tell you any more.

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.664
Let's see a clip.

00:07:45.664 --> 00:07:47.299
[ Machinery whirring,
tapping on metal ]

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:49.201
-There you hear that?

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:52.471
That is an S.O.S.

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:55.841
-Yeah, I hear. I just --
I just can't believe it.

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:58.010
-Thank you, Robert Forster.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.812
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.181
And that was a little unfair,
because, obviously,

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:03.649
I want you to come back
for "Corrections,"

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:05.217
but I do think we'll be showing

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:07.420
a new clip from
"Goliath Awaits."

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.055
1981, "Goliath Awaits."
It was two nights.

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:12.158
It was a two-night event.

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.326
Went back and read some reviews.

00:08:14.326 --> 00:08:16.629
They weren't great.

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:18.997
But sometimes...

00:08:18.997 --> 00:08:21.600
time helps great art.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.869
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:28.540
I referred to the Queen

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.609
as "our" monarch.

00:08:30.609 --> 00:08:34.847
You all pointed out
that she was not "my" monarch.

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:36.916
I should not have said "our."

00:08:36.916 --> 00:08:38.651
With one of you saying,
"Who knows?

00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:42.221
Maybe Seth just outed himself
as an undercover British spy."

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:44.990
To which I say...

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:47.459
[British accent]
Well, well, well.

00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:50.963
Looks like the game is up.

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:55.468
We've had a nice run,
though, haven't we, boys?

00:08:55.468 --> 00:08:58.270
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:01.640
if this is the end of things,
I don't mind.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.343
I go out drinking the queens.

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:09.849
I kept you on your back hills
long enough.

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:12.017
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.017 --> 00:09:14.386
Mispronounced certain words
to make you believe

00:09:14.386 --> 00:09:16.622
I was an American...

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.858
Nobel "laur-ee-ott."

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:22.261
[ Laughter ]

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:28.433
But now the game is over.

00:09:28.433 --> 00:09:29.935
[ Laughs ]

00:09:29.935 --> 00:09:32.871
[ Laughter ]

00:09:32.871 --> 00:09:37.910
I'm regretting my closing joke,
but I feel I'm part committed.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:41.080
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.415 --> 00:09:45.518
I want to make it clear
that this is a joke.

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:49.888
This is not a sponsorship.
It's just a closing joke.

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:53.692
[ Laughter ]
The game is up.

00:09:53.692 --> 00:09:57.496
Guess it's time to go home
and collect my "Twinnings."

00:09:57.496 --> 00:10:00.600
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.367 --> 00:10:03.569
[ Thud ]

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:05.571
[ Normal voice ]
See me next week.

